ps://github.com/apache/airflow/issues/72706#issuecomment-5616260682","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/72706","id":5616260682,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAgUK288AAAABTsFWSg","user":{"login":"hasansyed107","id":136695107,"node_id":"U_kgDOCCXNQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/136695107?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hasansyed107","html_url":"https://github.com/hasansyed107","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hasansyed107/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hasansyed107/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hasansyed107/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hasansyed107/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hasansyed107/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hasansyed107/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hasansyed107/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hasansyed107/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hasansyed107/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-10T09:23:07Z","updated_at":"2026-09-10T09:23:07Z","body":"Hi! I took a look at the current implementation, and it seems the team-scoped resource change spans several layers.\n\nFor Pool and Variable, the existing models already carry `team_name`, but their database uniqueness/lookups are still globally scoped. These seem like a relatively self-contained first step.\n\nThe Connection and especially DAG cases appear to have a larger impact because `dag_id` is currently part of the core identity/foreign-key model.\n\nWould it make sense to start by implementing team-scoped uniqueness and lookup semantics for Pool and Variable as a first PR, and handle the larger DAG/connection changes separately?\n\nIf that scope makes sense, I'd be happy to work on the first part.","author_association":"NONE"